<title>BOLIVIA: Bolivia's Sept inflation 0.16 pct.</title>
<headline>Bolivia's Sept inflation 0.16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LA PAZ 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bolivia's consumer prices rose 0.16 percent in September, down from 1.04 percent in August and 0.51 percent in September 1995, the National Statistics Institute said Thursday.</p>
<p>Prices rose 7.30 percent so far this year, up from 6.64 percent in the same period last year. Accumulated inflation in the 12 months to September was 13.28 percent.</p>
<p>The official inflation target for 1996 is 6.50 percent.</p>
<p>-- Carlos Quiroga, La Paz Newsroom +5912 39-1366</p>
